IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively): section 2035 of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2035), "Simplified
-- supplemental nutrition assistance program", lines 3057-3109 of usc07-ch51.txt (snap6's third range).
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the OLRC's USLM XML. It is not the official text, and
-- nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- READING A RESULT: a MAYBE BOOLEAN answers JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, JUST TRUE where it says
-- yes, and NOTHING everywhere else ("not covered"). Every branch says which kind it is.
-- Every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements (`s 2035(c)(1) ...`), and so does every
-- type and constructor, so that no two parts can share a name.
-- SEAMS: what other sections answer is taken as an input named for the answering section (SEAMS.md).

-- HELPERS (not a rule of the Act): three-valued AND / OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that a NOTHING input is passed through
-- unless another limb decides the answer without it (PLAN.md section 4).
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035 every one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) xs THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): one limb is the text's no, so the whole is, wherever that no came from
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb says no
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: every limb holds

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035 at least one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) xs THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: one limb holds
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every limb is the text's no

-- A duty-timing helper is not needed here: each timed duty below carries its own twin function.

§ `s 2035 -- Simplified supplemental nutrition assistance program`

-- TYPES this section needs (none is in the core).

-- (b) and (f): where, within the State, a Program is carried out.
DECLARE `s 2035 where the State elects` IS ONE OF
    `s 2035 statewide`
    `s 2035 in a political subdivision of the State`
    `s 2035 somewhere else`

-- (c)(4) and (f)(1): the rules and procedures a State uses to determine Program benefits.
DECLARE `s 2035 source of the benefit rules` IS ONE OF
    `s 2035 a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act`
    `s 2035 the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    `s 2035 a combination of the State TANF-funded program and the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    `s 2035 some other source`

-- (e): the acts the Secretary and the State agency are told to do (or not to do) when a Program increases Federal costs.
DECLARE `s 2035 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2035 determine whether the Program is increasing Federal costs`
    `s 2035 require the State agency to collect or report information on households not included in the Program`
    `s 2035 approve alternative accounting periods`
    `s 2035 notify the State that the Program has increased Federal costs`
    `s 2035 submit a plan for prompt corrective action`
    `s 2035 terminate the approval of the State agency operating the Program`

-- (f)(3): the seven groups of requirements a Program must still meet.
DECLARE `s 2035 requirement group` IS ONE OF
    `s 2035 subsections (a) through (f) of section 2016`
    `s 2035 section 2017(a)`
    `s 2035 subsections (b) and (d) of section 2017`
    `s 2035 subsections (a), (c), (d) and (n) of section 2020`
    `s 2035 paragraphs (8), (12), (15), (17), (18), (22) and (23) of section 2020(e)`
    `s 2035 section 2020(e)(10) or a comparable State TANF requirement`
    `s 2035 section 2025`

-- (f)(2): the three things a State shall consider in developing a standardized deduction.
DECLARE `s 2035 what the State considered` HAS
    `work expenses`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `dependent care costs`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `shelter costs`         IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `(a) "Federal costs" defined`

-- (a) a definition: "does not include" is a flat negative for costs incurred under section 2026; the text says nothing
-- else about what the term includes.
-- src:3058 | (a) “Federal costs” defined
-- src:3059 | In this section, the term “Federal costs” does not include any Federal costs incurred under section 2026 of this title.
@ref s 2035(a) "Federal costs" defined (src:3058-3059)
GIVEN `the cost was incurred under section 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(a) the cost is a Federal cost for this section` MEANS
    IF `the cost was incurred under section 2026`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include any Federal costs incurred under section 2026"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text only says what the term does not include

§§ `(b) Election`

-- (b) "Subject to subsection (d), a State may elect ... statewide or in a political subdivision": a grant to the State.
-- Operating the Program is separately conditioned by (d)(1).
-- src:3060 | (b) Election
-- src:3061 | Subject to subsection (d), a State may elect to carry out a simplified supplemental nutrition assistance program (referred to in this section as a “Program”), statewide or in a political subdivision of the State, in accordance with this section.
@ref s 2035(b) Election (src:3060-3061)
GIVEN `where the State would carry out the Program` IS A `s 2035 where the State elects`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(b) the State may elect to carry out a Program there` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the State would carry out the Program`
    WHEN `s 2035 statewide` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a State may elect to carry out a simplified supplemental nutrition assistance program ... statewide"
    WHEN `s 2035 in a political subdivision of the State` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "or in a political subdivision of the State"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names only statewide and a political subdivision

§§ `(c) Operation of Program`

-- (c)(1) "a household in which no members receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV ...
-- may not participate in the Program": a flat negative.
-- src:3062 | (c) Operation of Program
-- src:3063 | If a State elects to carry out a Program, within the State or a political subdivision of the State—
-- src:3064 | (1) a household in which no members receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) may not participate in the Program;
@ref s 2035(c)(1) a household with no member on a TANF-funded program (src:3062-3064)
GIVEN `members of the household` IS A NUMBER
      `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(c)(1) the household may participate in the Program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `members of the household` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not a household
        IF `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` GREATER THAN `members of the household` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the counts are inconsistent
        IF `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` EQUALS 0 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not participate in the Program"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (c)(1) speaks only of a household in which no member receives such assistance

-- (c)(2) "a household in which all members receive assistance ... shall automatically be eligible to participate".
-- src:3065 | (2) a household in which all members receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) shall automatically be eligible to participate in the Program;
@ref s 2035(c)(2) a household all of whose members are on a TANF-funded program (src:3065)
GIVEN `members of the household` IS A NUMBER
      `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(c)(2) the household is eligible to participate in the Program` MEANS
    IF `members of the household` AT LEAST 1 AND `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` EQUALS `members of the household`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall automatically be eligible to participate in the Program"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (c)(2) speaks only of a household in which all members receive such assistance

-- (c)(3) "if approved by the Secretary, a household in which 1 or more members but not all members receive assistance ...
-- may be eligible to participate": the Secretary's approval is a conditional input.
-- src:3066 | (3) if approved by the Secretary, a household in which 1 or more members but not all members receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) may be eligible to participate in the Program; and
@ref s 2035(c)(3) a household some but not all of whose members are on a TANF-funded program (src:3066)
GIVEN `members of the household` IS A NUMBER
      `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary has approved the household's participation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(c)(3) the household may be eligible to participate in the Program` MEANS
    IF `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` AT LEAST 1 AND `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` LESS THAN `members of the household`
    THEN CONSIDER `the Secretary has approved the household's participation`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "if approved by the Secretary, a household in which 1 or more members but not all members receive assistance ... may be eligible"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if approved by the Secretary" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no approval by the Secretary was supplied
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (c)(3) speaks only of a household in which some but not all members receive such assistance

-- (c) as a whole: which of (c)(1) to (c)(3) a household falls under.
-- src:3062 | (c) Operation of Program
-- src:3063 | If a State elects to carry out a Program, within the State or a political subdivision of the State—
-- src:3064 | (1) a household in which no members receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) may not participate in the Program;
-- src:3065 | (2) a household in which all members receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) shall automatically be eligible to participate in the Program;
-- src:3066 | (3) if approved by the Secretary, a household in which 1 or more members but not all members receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) may be eligible to participate in the Program; and
@ref s 2035(c) Operation of Program, paragraphs (1) to (3) (src:3062-3066)
GIVEN `members of the household` IS A NUMBER
      `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary has approved the household's participation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(c) the household may participate in the Program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `members of the household` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not a household
        IF `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` GREATER THAN `members of the household` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the counts are inconsistent
        IF `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` EQUALS 0
           THEN `s 2035(c)(1) the household may participate in the Program` `members of the household` `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV`
        IF `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` EQUALS `members of the household`
           THEN `s 2035(c)(2) the household is eligible to participate in the Program` `members of the household` `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV`
        OTHERWISE `s 2035(c)(3) the household may be eligible to participate in the Program` `members of the household` `members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` `the Secretary has approved the household's participation`

-- (c)(4) "subject to subsection (f), benefits under the Program shall be determined under rules and procedures established by
-- the State under (A), (B) or (C)": the three sources are named; the text does not close the list with "only".
-- src:3067 | (4) subject to subsection (f), benefits under the Program shall be determined under rules and procedures established by the State under—
-- src:3068 | (A) a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.);
-- src:3069 | (B) the supplemental nutrition assistance program; or
-- src:3070 | (C) a combination of a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) and the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2035(c)(4) rules and procedures for benefits (src:3067-3070)
GIVEN `the source of the rules and procedures` IS A `s 2035 source of the benefit rules`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(c)(4) benefits under the Program may be determined under rules from this source` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the source of the rules and procedures`
    WHEN `s 2035 a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(A) a State program funded under part A of title IV"
    WHEN `s 2035 the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(B) the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
    WHEN `s 2035 a combination of the State TANF-funded program and the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(C) a combination of"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text does not say "only" or "nothing but"

§§ `(d) Approval of Program`

-- (d)(1) "A State agency may not operate a Program unless the Secretary approves a State plan": an "unless", so a
-- missing approval is the text's no; an approval lifts the bar but grants nothing (the grant is in (b)).
-- src:3071 | (d) Approval of Program
-- src:3072 | (1) State plan
-- src:3073 | A State agency may not operate a Program unless the Secretary approves a State plan for the operation of the Program under paragraph (2).
@ref s 2035(d)(1) State plan (src:3071-3073)
GIVEN `the Secretary has approved a State plan under paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(d)(1) the State agency may operate a Program` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary has approved a State plan under paragraph (2)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State agency may not operate a Program unless the Secretary approves a State plan"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the "unless" lifts the bar; the grant to elect is in (b)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Secretary approved the plan was not supplied

-- (d)(2) "The Secretary shall approve any State plan ... if the Secretary determines that the plan (A) complies with this
-- section; and (B) contains sufficient documentation that the plan will not increase Federal costs for any fiscal year":
-- both determinations are the Secretary's, so both are conditional inputs.
-- src:3074 | (2) Approval of plan
-- src:3075 | The Secretary shall approve any State plan to carry out a Program if the Secretary determines that the plan—
-- src:3076 | (A) complies with this section; and
-- src:3077 | (B) contains sufficient documentation that the plan will not increase Federal costs for any fiscal year.
@ref s 2035(d)(2) Approval of plan (src:3074-3077)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that the plan complies with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the plan contains sufficient documentation that it will not increase Federal costs for any fiscal year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(d)(2) the Secretary shall approve the State plan` MEANS
    -- (A) and (B) are joined by "and"; a failed "if" is the text's no (marginal reading (a)); a NOTHING limb passes through
    -- unless the other limb decides the answer.
    `s 2035 every one of these holds` (LIST `the Secretary determines that the plan complies with this section`, `the Secretary determines that the plan contains sufficient documentation that it will not increase Federal costs for any fiscal year`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary determines that the plan (A) complies with this section; and (B) contains sufficient documentation" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a determination of the Secretary's was not supplied

§§ `(e) Increased Federal costs`

-- (e)(1)(A) "The Secretary shall determine whether a Program being carried out by a State agency is increasing Federal costs
-- under this chapter": a duty of the Secretary's with no time limit.
-- src:3078 | (e) Increased Federal costs
-- src:3079 | (1) Determination
-- src:3080 | (A) In general
-- src:3081 | The Secretary shall determine whether a Program being carried out by a State agency is increasing Federal costs under this chapter.
@ref s 2035(e)(1)(A) Determination (src:3078-3081)
`s 2035(e)(1)(A) the Secretary's duty to determine whether the Program is increasing Federal costs` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2035 determine whether the Program is increasing Federal costs`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not determine whether the Program is increasing Federal costs under this chapter"

-- (e)(1)(B) "the Secretary shall not require the State agency to collect or report any information on households not
-- included in the Program": a prohibition.
-- src:3082 | (B) No excluded households
-- src:3083 | In making a determination under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall not require the State agency to collect or report any information on households not included in the Program.
@ref s 2035(e)(1)(B) No excluded households (src:3082-3083)
`s 2035(e)(1)(B) the Secretary's prohibition on requiring information on households not in the Program` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    SHANT `s 2035 require the State agency to collect or report information on households not included in the Program`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary required the State agency to collect or report information on households not included in the Program"

-- (e)(1)(C) "The Secretary may approve the request of a State agency to apply alternative accounting periods": a permission.
-- src:3084 | (C) Alternative accounting periods
-- src:3085 | The Secretary may approve the request of a State agency to apply alternative accounting periods to determine if Federal costs do not exceed the Federal costs had the State agency not elected to carry out the Program.
@ref s 2035(e)(1)(C) Alternative accounting periods (src:3084-3085)
`s 2035(e)(1)(C) the Secretary's permission to approve alternative accounting periods` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2035 approve alternative accounting periods`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (e)(3)(B) "If the State does not submit a plan under subparagraph (A) or carry out a plan approved by the Secretary, the
-- Secretary shall terminate the approval of the State agency operating the Program and the State agency shall be ineligible
-- to operate a future Program." The duty (no time limit in the text) is written first so that (A) can point to it.
-- src:3091 | (B) Termination
-- src:3092 | If the State does not submit a plan under subparagraph (A) or carry out a plan approved by the Secretary, the Secretary shall terminate the approval of the State agency operating the Program and the State agency shall be ineligible to operate a future Program.
@ref s 2035(e)(3)(B) Termination (src:3091-3092)
`s 2035(e)(3)(B) the Secretary's duty to terminate the approval` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2035 terminate the approval of the State agency operating the Program`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not terminate the approval of the State agency operating the Program"

-- (e)(3)(A) "Not later than 90 days after the date of a notification under paragraph (2), the State shall submit a plan for
-- approval by the Secretary for prompt corrective action". If it does not, (B) follows.
-- src:3089 | (A) Corrective action
-- src:3090 | Not later than 90 days after the date of a notification under paragraph (2), the State shall submit a plan for approval by the Secretary for prompt corrective action that is designed to prevent the Program from increasing Federal costs under this chapter.
@ref s 2035(e)(3)(A) Corrective action (src:3089-3090)
`s 2035(e)(3)(A) the State's duty to submit a plan for prompt corrective action` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2035 submit a plan for prompt corrective action`
    WITHIN 90   -- days after the date of the notification under paragraph (2)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST `s 2035(e)(3)(B) the Secretary's duty to terminate the approval`

-- (e)(2) "the Secretary shall notify the State not later than 30 days after the Secretary makes the determination under
-- paragraph (1)", if the Secretary determines that the Program has increased Federal costs; then (3)(A) runs.
-- src:3086 | (2) Notification
-- src:3087 | If the Secretary determines that the Program has increased Federal costs under this chapter for any fiscal year or any portion of any fiscal year, the Secretary shall notify the State not later than 30 days after the Secretary makes the determination under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2035(e)(2) Notification (src:3086-3087)
`s 2035(e)(2) the Secretary's duty to notify the State` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2035 notify the State that the Program has increased Federal costs`
    WITHIN 30   -- days after the Secretary makes the determination under paragraph (1)
    HENCE `s 2035(e)(3)(A) the State's duty to submit a plan for prompt corrective action`
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not notify the State within 30 days after making the determination"

-- Twin of (e)(2) as a decision function over facts (a #TRACE outcome cannot be asserted on the stable binary).
-- The text: "the Secretary shall notify the State not later than 30 days after the Secretary makes the determination".
-- src:3086 | (2) Notification
-- src:3087 | If the Secretary determines that the Program has increased Federal costs under this chapter for any fiscal year or any portion of any fiscal year, the Secretary shall notify the State not later than 30 days after the Secretary makes the determination under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2035(e)(2) Notification (the twin over days) (src:3086-3087)
GIVEN `the Secretary has notified the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the determination to the notification, or to today if not yet notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(e)(2) the Secretary notified the State in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has notified the State` AND `days from the determination to the notification, or to today if not yet notified` AT MOST 30 THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "not later than 30 days after"
        IF `days from the determination to the notification, or to today if not yet notified` GREATER THAN 30 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 30 days after the Secretary makes the determination"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet notified and the 30 days have not run

-- Twin of (e)(3)(A): "Not later than 90 days after the date of a notification under paragraph (2)".
-- src:3089 | (A) Corrective action
-- src:3090 | Not later than 90 days after the date of a notification under paragraph (2), the State shall submit a plan for approval by the Secretary for prompt corrective action that is designed to prevent the Program from increasing Federal costs under this chapter.
@ref s 2035(e)(3)(A) Corrective action (the twin over days) (src:3089-3090)
GIVEN `the State has submitted a plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the notification to the submission, or to today if not yet submitted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(e)(3)(A) the State submitted its plan in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State has submitted a plan` AND `days from the notification to the submission, or to today if not yet submitted` AT MOST 90 THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Not later than 90 days after the date of a notification"
        IF `days from the notification to the submission, or to today if not yet submitted` GREATER THAN 90 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 90 days after the date of a notification"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet submitted and the 90 days have not run

-- (e)(3)(B) as a decision over facts: "If the State does not submit a plan ... or carry out a plan approved by the
-- Secretary, the Secretary shall terminate the approval ... and the State agency shall be ineligible to operate a future Program."
-- src:3091 | (B) Termination
-- src:3092 | If the State does not submit a plan under subparagraph (A) or carry out a plan approved by the Secretary, the Secretary shall terminate the approval of the State agency operating the Program and the State agency shall be ineligible to operate a future Program.
@ref s 2035(e)(3)(B) Termination (the decision) (src:3091-3092)
GIVEN `the State submitted a plan under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State carried out the plan the Secretary approved` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(e)(3)(B) the Secretary shall terminate the approval of the State agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State submitted a plan under subparagraph (A)` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "If the State does not submit a plan under subparagraph (A) ... the Secretary shall terminate the approval of the State agency"
        IF `the State carried out the plan the Secretary approved` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "or carry out a plan approved by the Secretary, the Secretary shall terminate"
        IF `the State carried out the plan the Secretary approved` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the State does not submit a plan ... or carry out a plan" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the State carried out the approved plan was not supplied

-- src:3091 | (B) Termination
-- src:3092 | If the State does not submit a plan under subparagraph (A) or carry out a plan approved by the Secretary, the Secretary shall terminate the approval of the State agency operating the Program and the State agency shall be ineligible to operate a future Program.
@ref s 2035(e)(3)(B) Termination (the State agency afterwards) (src:3091-3092)
GIVEN `the Secretary has terminated the approval of the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(e)(3)(B) the State agency may operate a future Program` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary has terminated the approval of the State agency`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the State agency shall be ineligible to operate a future Program"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (e)(3)(B) speaks only of a State agency whose approval was terminated

§§ `(f) Rules and procedures`

-- (f)(1) "a State or political subdivision of a State may follow the rules and procedures established ... under a State
-- program funded under part A of title IV ... or under the supplemental nutrition assistance program".
-- src:3094 | (1) In general
-- src:3095 | In operating a Program, a State or political subdivision of a State may follow the rules and procedures established by the State or political subdivision under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) or under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2035(f)(1) In general (src:3094-3095)
GIVEN `the source of the rules and procedures` IS A `s 2035 source of the benefit rules`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(f)(1) the State may follow the rules and procedures from this source` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the source of the rules and procedures`
    WHEN `s 2035 a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may follow the rules and procedures established ... under a State program funded under part A of title IV"
    WHEN `s 2035 the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "or under the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (f)(1) names two sources; a combination is dealt with in (c)(4)(C)

-- (f)(2) "may standardize the deductions provided under section 2014(e)".
-- src:3096 | (2) Standardized deductions
-- src:3097 | In operating a Program, a State or political subdivision of a State may standardize the deductions provided under section 2014(e) of this title. In developing the standardized deduction, the State shall consider the work expenses, dependent care costs, and shelter costs of participating households.
@ref s 2035(f)(2) Standardized deductions (src:3096-3097)
GIVEN `the deduction is one provided under section 2014(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(f)(2) the State may standardize the deduction` MEANS
    IF `the deduction is one provided under section 2014(e)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may standardize the deductions provided under section 2014(e)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of the deductions provided under section 2014(e)

-- (f)(2) second sentence: "In developing the standardized deduction, the State shall consider the work expenses,
-- dependent care costs, and shelter costs of participating households."
-- src:3097 | In operating a Program, a State or political subdivision of a State may standardize the deductions provided under section 2014(e) of this title. In developing the standardized deduction, the State shall consider the work expenses, dependent care costs, and shelter costs of participating households.
@ref s 2035(f)(2) the State shall consider three things (src:3097)
GIVEN `what the State considered` IS A `s 2035 what the State considered`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(f)(2) the State has considered what it shall consider` MEANS
    IF `what the State considered`'s `work expenses` AND `what the State considered`'s `dependent care costs` AND `what the State considered`'s `shelter costs`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the State shall consider the work expenses, dependent care costs, and shelter costs of participating households"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states the duty but not what follows if one of the three is left out

-- (f)(3) "In operating a Program, a State or political subdivision shall comply with the requirements of (A) to (G)":
-- each group's compliance is a section 2016, 2017, 2020 or 2025 answer, taken as a conditional input.
-- src:3098 | (3) Requirements
-- src:3099 | In operating a Program, a State or political subdivision shall comply with the requirements of—
-- src:3100 | (A) subsections (a) through (f) of section 2016 of this title;
-- src:3101 | (B) section 2017(a) of this title (except that the income of a household may be determined under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.));
-- src:3102 | (C) subsections (b) and (d) of section 2017 of this title;
-- src:3103 | (D) subsections (a), (c), (d), and (n) of section 2020 of this title;
-- src:3104 | (E) paragraphs (8), (12), (15), (17), (18), (22), and (23) of section 2020(e) of this title;
-- src:3105 | (F) section 2020(e)(10) of this title (or a comparable requirement established by the State under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.)); and
-- src:3106 | (G) section 2025 of this title.
@ref s 2035(f)(3) Requirements (src:3098-3106)
GIVEN `s 2016(a) to (f) the State meets the requirements of subsections (a) through (f) of section 2016` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2017(a) the State meets the requirements of section 2017(a), leaving aside how the household's income was determined` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2017(b) and (d) the State meets the requirements of subsections (b) and (d) of section 2017` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2020(a), (c), (d) and (n) the State meets the requirements of those subsections of section 2020` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2020(e) the State meets the requirements of paragraphs (8), (12), (15), (17), (18), (22) and (23) of section 2020(e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2020(e)(10) the State meets section 2020(e)(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State meets a comparable requirement established under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2025 the State meets the requirements of section 2025` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(f)(3) the State complies with the requirements it shall comply with` MEANS
    `s 2035 every one of these holds`
        (LIST `s 2016(a) to (f) the State meets the requirements of subsections (a) through (f) of section 2016`,
              `s 2017(a) the State meets the requirements of section 2017(a), leaving aside how the household's income was determined`,
              `s 2017(b) and (d) the State meets the requirements of subsections (b) and (d) of section 2017`,
              `s 2020(a), (c), (d) and (n) the State meets the requirements of those subsections of section 2020`,
              `s 2020(e) the State meets the requirements of paragraphs (8), (12), (15), (17), (18), (22) and (23) of section 2020(e)`,
              `s 2035 at least one of these holds` (LIST `s 2020(e)(10) the State meets section 2020(e)(10)`, `the State meets a comparable requirement established under a State program funded under part A of title IV`),
              `s 2025 the State meets the requirements of section 2025`)
    -- This answers "has the State met every requirement group in (f)(3)". It never answers JUST FALSE from the text's own
    -- words: a group not met is a fact about another section; the answer then is JUST FALSE only because a group's own
    -- answer (from the answering section) is JUST FALSE. The function adds no "no" of its own.

-- (f)(3)(B) the parenthesis: "(except that the income of a household may be determined under a State program funded under part A".
-- src:3101 | (B) section 2017(a) of this title (except that the income of a household may be determined under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.));
@ref s 2035(f)(3)(B) the exception for income (src:3101)
GIVEN `the source of the rules and procedures` IS A `s 2035 source of the benefit rules`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(f)(3)(B) the household's income may be determined under this source` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the source of the rules and procedures`
    WHEN `s 2035 a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the income of a household may be determined under a State program funded under part A of title IV"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception names one source

-- (f)(4) "a household may not receive benefits under this section as a result of the eligibility of the household under a
-- State program funded under part A of title IV ..., unless the Secretary determines that any household with income above 130
-- percent of the poverty guidelines is not eligible for the program."
-- src:3107 | (4) Limitation on eligibility
-- src:3108 | Notwithstanding any other provision of this section, a household may not receive benefits under this section as a result of the eligibility of the household under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), unless the Secretary determines that any household with income above 130 percent of the poverty guidelines is not eligible for the program.
@ref s 2035(f)(4) Limitation on eligibility (src:3107-3108)
GIVEN `the Secretary has determined that no household with income above 130 percent of the poverty guidelines is eligible for the State program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2035(f)(4) the household may receive benefits under this section as a result of its eligibility under the State program` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary has determined that no household with income above 130 percent of the poverty guidelines is eligible for the State program`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a household may not receive benefits under this section as a result of the eligibility of the household under a State program funded under part A of title IV ..., unless the Secretary determines"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the "unless" lifts the bar and grants nothing by itself
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
